Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:50:29 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Mac: Chromium's tab menu in the unified strip

Right-clicking a tab of the unified strip shows Chromium's own tab menu
(TabMenuModel) for the tab in its window, with a Plurium submenu for
what the profiles add: Move to <profile>, Profile Color and Close Other
Tabs of <profile>. The tab position toggle (Show Tabs Vertically), Mute
Site, Reading List and extension items now work from the strip too.

New Tab to the Right and Duplicate place the new tab right after the
clicked one in the unified order and show its window; Close Other Tabs
and Close Tabs to the Right close the other tabs or the tabs after it in
the unified order, of all profiles. Pin, groups, split view and moving a
tab to another window are left out until the strip can show them.
